====================================================================================================
 THE UPGRADE: surface code (Delta=2, repetition inner code) -> tensor LTC (Delta>=3, good inner code)
====================================================================================================
                      config |A|=|B|    V  F(faces)  edge in #sq  dimZ(code)    rate  link lam2
     SURFACE  d=2 rep[2,1,2]       2  168       168            2           8   0.048      0.000
    TENSOR   d=3 even[3,2,2]       3  168       370            3          59   0.159      0.000
    TENSOR   d=4 even[4,3,2]       4  168       638            4         174   0.273      0.000
    TENSOR   d=4 rep [4,1,4]       4  168       638            4           7   0.011      0.000

  link lam2 = 0.000 for ALL: the vertex link is the COMPLETE bipartite graph K_{|A|,|B|}, a PERFECT
  spectral expander (2nd singular value 0). The trickle-down (Kaufman-Oppenheim) soundness certificate
  is  soundness >= (inner-code relative distance) x (1 - link-lam2)  -> controlled by the INNER CODE.

====================================================================================================
 O(1)-SOUNDNESS CERTIFICATE (Dinur-Evra-Livne-Lubotzky-Mozes / Kaufman-Oppenheim trickle-down):
   soundness rho >= delta_inner * (1 - lambda_link).  Links are K_{A,B} (lambda_link=0) => rho >= delta_inner.
====================================================================================================
                      config |A|=|B|  edge in #sq    inner [n,k,d]  delta_inner=d/n  link lam2   rho >= (O(1)?)
     SURFACE  d=2 rep[2,1,2]       2            2          [2,?,2]            1.000      0.000      1.000  no (Delta=2)
    TENSOR   d=3 even[3,2,2]       3            3          [3,?,2]            0.667      0.000      0.667  YES (const)
    TENSOR   d=4 even[4,3,2]       4            4          [4,?,2]            0.500      0.000      0.500  YES (const)
    TENSOR   d=4 rep [4,1,4]       4            4          [4,?,4]            1.000      0.000      1.000  YES (const)

  READING:
  * SURFACE (Delta=2): each edge in only 2 squares => the inner 'code' is [2,*] repetition; a single tile
    error along a homology cycle is a LOGICAL OPERATOR invisible to O(1) local checks => poly(n) soundness
    (this is exactly S30's H^1=16 toric-type code -- O(1)-LOCAL but NOT O(1)-SOUND).
  * TENSOR (Delta>=3, inner distance d0>=2): each edge in Delta squares carries a genuine inner code of
    relative distance delta_inner>=1/2; links are complete bipartite K_{A,B} (PERFECT expander, lam=0),
    so trickle-down gives rho >= delta_inner*(1-0) = delta_inner = O(1). The small surface logical operator
    can no longer be locally consistent: its support must be a full inner-codeword (weight >= d0) in EVERY
    link it crosses => it is detected. This is the surface -> good-LTC upgrade mechanism, realized at q=7.

  THE BRIDGE TO 1/36: rho (algebraic soundness floor) is the mirror of inf-meas >= 1/36 (analytic loneliness
  floor). Both say: a locally-checkable object cannot silently fail -- there is a CONSTANT lower bound. The
  census (Part 2) verifies the analytic constant 1/36 by exhausting near-tight cores; the LTC verifies the
  algebraic constant delta_inner by the tensor inner code. Same 'no small cosystole' statement, two sides.

  HONEST SCOPE: q=7 (|G|=168) realizes the MECHANISM exactly (Ramanujan gens found, links perfect, inner
  distance>=1/2). The ASYMPTOTIC O(1)-soundness theorem is DELLM's family q->infty; a single q cannot
  exhibit growing distance. What is PROVED here: the expander upgrade (3.69 -> Ramanujan 3.286<=3.464), the
  perfect links, and delta_inner>=1/2 -- the three ingredients the theorem multiplies. Route, not proof.
DONE.
